ATLAS Collaboration have also published fiducial and differential cross section measurements of Higgs boson production  in the four-lepton decay 
channel~\cite{ATLAS:H4l_8TeV}. These measurements are performed using collision data corresponding to integrated luminosity of 20.3~\ifb at $\sqrt{s} = 8$~TeV. 
Both measurements, ATLAS and CMS, are similar except few smaller differences mentioned below 
\begin{itemize}
 
 \item The measurements have been extracted assuming $m_H =  125.0 (125.4)$~GeV by CMS (ATLAS), as measured using the $H \rightarrow 2\gamma$ and
 $H \rightarrow 4\ell$ decay channels by the both experiment~\cite{Reference39,Aad:ATLAS_mass_measurement}.
 \item Small differences in  selections cut used to define  fiducial volume
 \item No requirement on Gen level isolation in case of ATLAS and does not provide model dependence like CMS.

 \end{itemize}

The differential results results are also produced as a function of production and decay related observables ( same observables except  an additional observable 
(Y(H)- Y(leading jet) chosen by CMS ). Figure \ref{fig:ATLAS_differential-bins-2} shows the differential cross section results as function of differential 
observables. The inclusive fiducial production cross section is measured to be 
$\sigma_{{\rm fid.}}^{{\rem tot.}}=2.11^{+0.53}_{-0.47}$(stat.)$\pm 0.08$(syst.) fb while the theoretical prediction at estimated for Higgs boson mass of 125.4~GeV
is $1.30\pm0.13$~fb. Both ATLAS and CMS measurements are found to be compatible with theoretical estimations and no significant deviation has been observed. 
The p-value are obtained for differential observables N(jets) ( largest deviation from SM in case of the CMS) is $p=0.13 (0.37)$ for the CMS (ATLAS) measurements.
